# component: alert
# decisions: A11Y-3, A11Y-8, A11Y-13, API-29, COL-12, DOC-2, LAY-15
# hunks:
#   API-29: each status variant gives every non-primary button inside it the family's own hover
#     and open state (`bg-<family>/10 text-<family>-text`, the svg too), keyed on Button's
#     `data-variant`; the neutral `bg-muted text-foreground` hover read white in dark mode on a
#     destructive alert. `contrast-check.mjs` gates the pair in both themes (MK, 2026-09-25).
#     Amended (MK, 2026-10-08): an outline button also takes `border-<family>/40 text-<family>-text`
#     at rest.
#   LAY-15 (MK, 2026-09-24): the root becomes an `@container/alert` grid whose action gets its own
#     trailing column (`[1fr_auto]`, `[auto_1fr_auto]` with an icon) from `@md` up, with the title
#     and description pinned to the text column; `AlertAction` loses `absolute top-2 end-2` for
#     `row-span-2 self-start` in that column, and below `@md` it drops under the text. Upstream's
#     `pe-18` reserve goes: an `sm` label over seven characters overlapped the title.
#     Amended (MK, 2026-09-30): `AlertAction` is a `flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2` row, so two
#     buttons sit side by side with the button-group gap and wrap when the alert is narrow.
#     Amended (MK, 2026-10-08): padding is `px-3 py-2.5`; with an action and no `AlertTitle` (from
#     `@md`) the description takes `min-h-8 content-center` and the icon `translate-y-2`, so a
#     single line sits centred on the 32px button and longer text stays top-aligned.
#   COL-12: `success`, `warning` and `info` variants, written in upstream's own `destructive`
#     shape (one ink, a dimmed description). Amended (MK, 2026-10-08): every status variant
#     paints `border-<family>/30` over a `bg-<family>/5` tint (`/10` in dark) instead of `bg-card`;
#     `default` keeps the neutral border and card. The four status families exist in the
#     token contract; Alert is where they surface as a banner.
#   A11Y-13: every status variant takes the family's `-text` ink rather than the fill. Upstream's
#     `text-destructive` on card measures 3.98:1 in light, under the AA floor A11Y-1 enforces.
#   A11Y-8: status is never colour alone — the docs page and `alert.test.tsx` require an icon
#     and a title beside the tint; the class string reserves the icon column either way.
#   A11Y-3 (assigned to alert by MK 2026-09-24, Regent #138 D1): `Alert` takes `live?: boolean`
#     (default `false`, not forwarded to the DOM). The root is a polite `role="status"` for every
#     variant, and takes upstream's assertive `role="alert"` only when `live` is set AND the variant
#     is `destructive` or `warning` — content that appeared after mount because of something the
#     user did. A caller's own `role` still wins, as it did over upstream's.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file; those hunks carry no decision of their own.
